Unfortunately, there's nothing useful within the oprofile output. If you're
serious about trying to track down the cause of CPU usage, I would suggest
trying to see if one of the X apps can result in a CPU usage spike. Even
better, if you have a small program to show a problem.

For example, if you have some benchmarks over a series of time that show the
driver operating worse after a particular version. That would allow the
maintainers to revert whatever change caused increased CPU + mem use.

If you get something more concrete, feel free to open a new bug.

